---
import { ChevronDown as ChevronDownIcon } from "@lucide/astro";
---

<!-- FAQ Section -->
<section id="faq" class="py-16 md:py-24">
	<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
		<div class="text-center mb-16">
			<span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-400"
				>Frequently Asked Questions</span
			>
			<h2
				class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight mt-2"
			>
				Clear answers to common questions
			</h2>
		</div>

		<div class="space-y-4">
			<!-- Q1 -->
			<details
				class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900 p-5 open:bg-slate-900/90 transition-colors"
			>
				<summary
					class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none text-sm font-semibold text-white"
				>
					<span>How does the tool ensure privacy and local execution?</span>
					<span class="text-slate-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">
						<ChevronDownIcon class="w-5 h-5 faq-chevron" />
					</span>
				</summary>
				<p
					class="mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed border-t border-slate-800/80 pt-3"
				>
					Yes, 100%. The application operates completely locally on your computer. It makes no
					outbound connections to external relays, servers, or analytics services. All
					activity runs strictly client-side, and results are kept solely in the local
					<code class="text-slate-300 font-mono text-xs">results/</code> folder on your
					machine.
				</p>
			</details>

			<!-- Q2 -->
			<details
				class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900 p-5 open:bg-slate-900/90 transition-colors"
			>
				<summary
					class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none text-sm font-semibold text-white"
				>
					<span>How does the automated browser handle verification prompts?</span>
					<span class="text-slate-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">
						<ChevronDownIcon class="w-5 h-5 faq-chevron" />
					</span>
				</summary>
				<p
					class="mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed border-t border-slate-800/80 pt-3"
				>
					During educational onboarding, the platform sends a confirmation message to your
					mailbox to verify ownership. The desktop app pauses cleanly and presents an
					interactive prompt with input sanitization. Once you submit the confirmation,
					automation resumes immediately.
				</p>
			</details>

			<!-- Q3 -->
			<details
				class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900 p-5 open:bg-slate-900/90 transition-colors"
			>
				<summary
					class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none text-sm font-semibold text-white"
				>
					<span>Why does Google One require verification during promotional activation?</span>
					<span class="text-slate-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">
						<ChevronDownIcon class="w-5 h-5 faq-chevron" />
					</span>
				</summary>
				<p
					class="mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed border-t border-slate-800/80 pt-3"
				>
					This is a standard Google One subscription requirement. Google One subscription
					policy requires establishing promotional eligibility.
					<strong>You are billed $0.00 today</strong> for the promotional tier. You can easily
					manage or disable recurring preferences in your Google account settings at any
					point.
				</p>
			</details>

			<!-- Q4 -->
			<details
				class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900 p-5 open:bg-slate-900/90 transition-colors"
			>
				<summary
					class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none text-sm font-semibold text-white"
				>
					<span>What if a Cloudflare or reCAPTCHA verification challenge appears?</span>
					<span class="text-slate-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">
						<ChevronDownIcon class="w-5 h-5 faq-chevron" />
					</span>
				</summary>
				<p
					class="mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed border-t border-slate-800/80 pt-3"
				>
					The engine proactively monitors for interstitial challenges. If one occurs,
					automation safely pauses to prevent lockouts, allowing you to resolve the prompt in
					the browser before continuing.
				</p>
			</details>

			<!-- Q5 -->
			<details
				class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900 p-5 open:bg-slate-900/90 transition-colors"
			>
				<summary
					class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none text-sm font-semibold text-white"
				>
					<span>Do I need to install Python, Node, or Playwright browser binaries?</span>
					<span class="text-slate-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">
						<ChevronDownIcon class="w-5 h-5 faq-chevron" />
					</span>
				</summary>
				<p
					class="mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed border-t border-slate-800/80 pt-3"
				>
					No. When using the standalone portable application (<code
						class="text-slate-300 font-mono text-xs"
						>Google AI Plus Portal</code
					>), all dependencies are bundled into the binary. It automatically attaches to your
					existing Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge, or Brave browser without requiring external
					browser downloads.
				</p>
			</details>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
